00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:47.010
His biggest beef in life is not knowing where the TV guy it is.

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.930
All right, that's my biggest beef. I've got my...

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:53.280
Mom, oh, shoot.

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:55.380
Well, you know that book, that book I wrote on it.

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:57.060
Oh, honey, you know I'm a little worried about you, though.

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:57.420
Yeah?

00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:58.900
You look haggard.

00:17:59.100 --> 00:17:59.380
I do.

00:17:59.580 --> 00:17:59.980
You really do.

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:00.970
I'm gonna go.

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:02.070
I saw a

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:04.710
Uh, picture you on the cover of some magazine.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:07.070
Oh, yeah, that was your Time magazine.

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:08.830
Mickey Hart subscribes to that.

00:18:08.950 --> 00:18:10.710
He brings it into the shop before he throws it away.

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:11.230
Here we go again.

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:13.270
Another chapter on Mickey Hart.

00:18:13.750 --> 00:18:15.430
Can you forget him?

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:18.900
Could you, Ed, could you do that one little thing for my sanity?

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:20.970
Thank you.

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:23.600
Besides, it wasn't Time Magazine anyway.

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:26.780
I mean, what in the hell would I be doing reading time?

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:29.980
Anyway, your picture.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.060
was on cover of this magazine and I just happened to catch my eye

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:35.400
when I was over there at the mall.

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:37.140
It was on Newsweek, too, you know.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.420
It was on Newsweek, too.

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:40.800
Newsweek, well, maybe it was Newsweek, but I don't know.

00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:43.280
I didn't like it because your eyes were all puffy

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:45.040
and your face was all thin and drawn.

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:47.560
Well, you know, that wasn't a picture.

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:48.460
That was a drawing.

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:49.560
It was a caricature.

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:51.400
Well, whatever it was, you looked awful.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:55.000
I mean, I was embarrassed to tell anybody you was my brother.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:06.810
Okay.

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:09.420
I love your hair.

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:10.960
Oh, you couldn't possibly.

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:11.700
It's filthy.

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:14.360
Eunice told you to say that now, didn't she?

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:15.360
Oh, no, no, no, no, she didn't.

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:15.920
No, no, she didn't.

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:16.400
I swear, I swear.

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:19.480
Come rain or shine, I get my hair done every Friday

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:20.420
at 3 o'clock.

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:21.820
But last Friday, no.

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.240
That sister of yours there has to pawn off those two

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:25.880
little holy terrors of hers on me.

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:27.780
All you had to do was say no, Mama.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:29.960
Well, you said you'd be back here at 2.30, you know what?

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:34.060
you got back here? I couldn't help it if Dr. Hanson kept me waiting for an hour and a half.

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:38.670
3.50. I go to church Sunday with my hair filthy. It's a wonder they let me in the door.

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:48.320
Dr. Hanson's a quack anyway. He is not a quack. Well, I wouldn't take my dog to him.

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:55.430
You have to meet Topaz. Who? Topaz, he is the cutest little French

00:19:55.430 --> 00:19:59.590
poodle we got mama for her birthday. Smart as a whip, too. Just like my dog.

00:19:59.590 --> 00:19:59.970
I'm going to-

00:20:11.580 --> 00:20:13.320
on the foot of my bed after his lunchie.

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:16.700
Except he hadn't been doing his business at all, right?

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:20.360
Mama passing.

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:22.860
Ed and I had the same trouble with the boys.

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:25.320
Well, it sure is odd you never did tell me.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:27.800
Well, for Pete's sakes, why rile you up?

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:29.020
I knew it was passing.

00:20:30.960 --> 00:20:33.500
That's all. I mean, you and Phillip never had any problem that way,

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:34.600
unless they can build them.

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:42.840
No, no, Mom. Everything is just fine in that department.

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:45.450
Well, why don't you just sit right down over here, Phillip,

00:20:45.570 --> 00:20:47.110
and tell me all about India.

00:20:47.190 --> 00:20:47.470
All right.

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:50.650
Now, why do they let those cows just run all over the street there

00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:51.590
and do anything they want?

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:53.070
Oh, you see, Mom, they're sacred.

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:55.230
That's a tradition that goes back to a century after...

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:55.670
Shh, listen, listen, listen.

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:58.490
Mama found Topaz. He's in your bedroom.

00:20:58.630 --> 00:20:59.970
You have got to come in here and see...

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:02.980
He's the cutest thing you have. Keep it quiet though.

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:04.240
What's that little Dickens doing?

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:08.480
He's looking up on those high ladies in the middle of my pillows,

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:10.900
looking out the back window. What is he looking at?

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:12.180
What is he looking at?

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:13.560
I can't believe that dog.

00:21:18.950 --> 00:21:20.450
You frightened Topaz.

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:21.830
He ran into the bathroom.

00:21:21.970 --> 00:21:24.030
Now I bet he won't even come out and say hello.

00:21:24.350 --> 00:21:26.910
Of course he will. Now if we all just sit down and ignore him,

00:21:26.990 --> 00:21:28.250
he'll be out here before you know it,

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:29.250
saying, what in the world?

00:21:53.530 --> 00:21:55.590
I'd love to take you on a trip to Europe with me

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.940
on my good antique table.

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:03.600
Well, that's so much as a dough in London.

00:22:03.720 --> 00:22:05.100
Would you look at the rain that left there?

00:22:05.280 --> 00:22:08.140
I bet you don't treat that Danish modern junk of yours like that.

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:11.420
Oh, Phil, you just gotta stay over one night and see our new house.

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:14.400
Oh, you know, I'm sorry. I can't. I gotta catch that plane to London tonight.

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:15.900
I've got this interview with Princess Anne.

00:22:15.940 --> 00:22:16.620
Well, put it up.

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:19.450
I can't. She's arranged a schedule, everything.

00:22:19.790 --> 00:22:22.370
Why aren't you interviewing the Queen? She too uppity to talk to you?

00:22:22.810 --> 00:22:24.550
Well, no, Mom. You see, the book that I'm writing...

00:22:24.550 --> 00:22:27.090
You know, Phil, what I want to know is, uh,

00:22:27.090 --> 00:22:29.980
Is Prince Charles really in love with, uh...

00:22:30.760 --> 00:22:34.820
What's her name? You know, uh, Grace Kelly's daughter, uh, Caroline, mama.

00:22:35.100 --> 00:22:36.320
Caroline, are you sure?

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:45.020
Time Magazine, they never even met.

00:22:45.230 --> 00:22:51.130
Oh, well, seems to me like Mickey Hurt's subscription to Time Magazine sure does keep you up on the news.

00:22:51.530 --> 00:22:57.600
Will the two of you please shut up? Charlie.

00:22:58.780 --> 00:22:59.320
Let me see, mom.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.540
I'm afraid I don't know too much about them.

00:23:01.640 --> 00:23:04.280
You see, I've been in India writing that Pulitzer Prize.

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:14.840
So quick, you're going to stick with this writing game.

00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:20.740
Well, yeah, I figure I might just as well give it a whirl a little while longer.

00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:21.880
Come on, now.

00:23:21.980 --> 00:23:24.260
I mean, it really isn't steady now, though, is it?

00:23:24.850 --> 00:23:25.710
You know what?

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:29.870
I bet you if you wanted to, you could wangle yourself a column or something, right?

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:31.670
on the Raytown Morning Star.

00:23:31.850 --> 00:23:32.850
There's a job for you.

00:23:33.190 --> 00:23:34.910
Then you wouldn't have to keep gallivanting

00:23:34.910 --> 00:23:36.870
all over the world and burying yourself

00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:38.350
in places like India.

00:23:38.690 --> 00:23:41.530
India is fascinating, Uni.

00:23:41.710 --> 00:23:43.390
I mean, you meet the most interesting characters.

00:23:43.590 --> 00:23:45.330
Characters? You want to meet characters, honey?

00:23:45.410 --> 00:23:47.670
All you've got to do is walk down the main street

00:23:47.670 --> 00:23:49.970
of Raytown any time of the day

00:23:49.970 --> 00:23:51.710
or night, because we have got them.

00:23:51.830 --> 00:23:52.330
Isn't that right, Andy?

00:23:52.330 --> 00:23:54.550
Oh, do we? Phil, do you know

00:23:54.550 --> 00:23:57.080
we got a bald woman right here

00:23:57.080 --> 00:23:57.740
on this block?

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:07.490
is bald, she ain't got a hair on her head. Boy, howdy, I'd like to write about her.

00:24:08.150 --> 00:24:12.030
Writing your way out of a paper bag fills the only one in the family with any talent.

00:24:17.570 --> 00:24:26.890
Well, I had other talents, mama. Took piano and voice, didn't I? Whenever we had company

00:24:26.890 --> 00:24:29.610
over, you always asked me to sing and play, didn't you?

00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:38.020
not you did so and don't you walk out on me like that you did too and you know it i did too i used

00:24:38.020 --> 00:24:39.490
to i used to do turk

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:04.260
in high school and I know what you're saying.

00:25:10.150 --> 00:25:11.510
Well, you see what that little dick was told to him.

00:25:11.510 --> 00:25:12.270
What you doing, Mom?

00:25:20.700 --> 00:25:22.600
Dang, he's going to get it, I'm telling you.

00:25:22.740 --> 00:25:23.700
Don't believe that, dog.

00:25:23.860 --> 00:25:24.400
I can't hear you.

00:25:24.620 --> 00:25:25.820
Look at him in the little tail, Joe.

00:25:26.120 --> 00:25:26.220
Don't get it.

00:25:27.300 --> 00:25:28.200
He is a character.

00:25:28.280 --> 00:25:29.080
He really gets it.

00:25:29.080 --> 00:25:29.860
I swan, he.

00:25:33.640 --> 00:25:36.440
Well, Mom, I think I'd better get along.

00:25:36.660 --> 00:25:37.740
It's quite a way to the airport.

00:25:37.940 --> 00:25:38.840
I don't want to miss that plane.

00:25:39.000 --> 00:25:41.040
Phil, I understand you do what you got to do

00:25:41.040 --> 00:25:42.260
because you're a busy working man.

00:25:42.340 --> 00:25:43.760
It sure was nice seeing you again.

00:25:43.860 --> 00:25:45.180
It sure was, honey.

00:25:45.280 --> 00:25:47.640
And don't make it so long between visits.

00:25:47.760 --> 00:25:48.740
Good seeing you, Phil.

00:25:48.820 --> 00:25:49.980
You come on. I'll back here.

00:25:50.140 --> 00:25:50.760
Come on back.

00:25:51.160 --> 00:25:52.420
Don't go back here that way.

00:25:52.440 --> 00:25:53.120
No, I believe you.

00:25:53.140 --> 00:25:54.400
I think he's looking at a barn.

00:25:57.300 --> 00:25:59.540
Hey, Mom!

00:26:00.120 --> 00:26:02.220
Would you like me to send you a copy of my new book?

00:26:02.410 --> 00:26:03.690
Oh, you don't have to do that, Phil.

00:26:03.830 --> 00:26:06.210
Besides, I got so many books now, I don't know where to put them.

00:26:08.970 --> 00:26:09.810
He's a cutie.

00:26:09.830 --> 00:26:11.220
Well, so long.

00:26:15.710 --> 00:26:17.880
Phil, make sure you close that screen door after you.

00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:20.020
Yeah, honey, the fly's gonna get on the lemonade.

00:26:20.960 --> 00:26:24.920
Oh, Phil, be sure and get rid of them puffy eyes.

00:26:26.900 --> 00:26:27.520
I'll try.

00:26:27.820 --> 00:26:29.240
You just look at that dog.

00:26:29.240 --> 00:26:29.760
Look at him now.

00:26:30.410 --> 00:26:31.890
I'll tell you, he's you.

00:26:32.150 --> 00:26:33.090
I'll tell you, that guy's you.

00:26:49.720 --> 00:26:50.580
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:26:51.820 --> 00:26:53.220
Oh, I cut the other tongue.

00:27:02.110 --> 00:27:03.870
That's, that's what I found.

00:27:06.200 --> 00:27:18.880
Look at me.

00:27:19.280 --> 00:27:19.940
What's the matter, Charlie?

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:21.260
You have a fight with Mrs. Olsen?

00:27:22.340 --> 00:27:27.000
See, you stopped off at the truck and got some coffee, too, huh?

00:27:27.200 --> 00:27:29.140
Yeah, but I plan to drink mine.

00:27:31.080 --> 00:27:34.760
Hey, did you notice they even got a dame diving that truck now?

00:27:35.060 --> 00:27:36.180
Yeah, I saw that.

00:27:36.630 --> 00:27:38.430
That's something about those dames moving in everywhere.

00:27:39.200 --> 00:27:40.640
Wouldn't it be something if that new helper

00:27:40.640 --> 00:27:42.360
they're sending over today turns out to be one?

00:27:42.860 --> 00:27:43.960
Get out of here.

00:27:44.660 --> 00:27:47.420
Can you imagine a broad building a house?

00:27:48.160 --> 00:27:50.640
First thing they'd want to put up would be the curtains.

00:27:52.530 --> 00:27:54.430
First thing she'd build would be the garage,

00:27:54.690 --> 00:27:56.150
have a place to send you to smoke.

00:27:57.090 --> 00:27:58.490
Hey, I can just see me working with a chick.

00:27:58.730 --> 00:27:59.870
Oh, excuse me.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:00.640
I'm gonna back up.

00:28:00.980 --> 00:28:03.780
Would you help me saw this 2x4 in half?

00:28:05.110 --> 00:28:06.570
Oh, not thou, I have headaches.

00:28:09.020 --> 00:28:10.760
I got nothing to worry about on that score.

00:28:11.020 --> 00:28:13.400
Why, they wouldn't even be able to carry a toolbox.

00:28:19.030 --> 00:28:21.490
With that hot coffee, you almost burned your bra.

00:28:24.920 --> 00:28:25.440
I'm waiting for you.

00:28:25.940 --> 00:28:27.420
You're a carpenter?

00:28:27.930 --> 00:28:28.770
Well, yes, I am.

00:28:29.380 --> 00:28:29.940
Oh, boy.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:30.940
Oh my God.

00:28:31.270 --> 00:28:32.650
I'll tell you one thing right now, sister.

00:28:32.770 --> 00:28:34.290
You're gonna have to pull your own weight around here.

00:28:34.390 --> 00:28:34.590
Yeah.

00:28:34.930 --> 00:28:36.130
Can you handle a rip saw?

00:28:36.650 --> 00:28:37.370
Yes, I can.

00:28:37.900 --> 00:28:38.600
Oh, you can, huh?

00:28:38.720 --> 00:28:38.960
Yes.

00:28:39.180 --> 00:28:40.400
Oh, we got to cut all those boards

00:28:40.400 --> 00:28:41.900
and put them up on that wall over there.

00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:43.360
Yeah, for the next eight hours, there's

00:28:43.360 --> 00:28:45.400
going to be a lot of ripping and banging around here.

00:28:45.460 --> 00:28:46.340
You sure you can handle it?

00:28:50.150 --> 00:28:50.290
All right.

00:28:50.920 --> 00:28:51.420
Let's get started.

00:28:51.980 --> 00:28:52.780
Hand me that board.

00:28:54.360 --> 00:28:56.000
Hand you the board? What's the matter? You pregnant?

00:28:56.550 --> 00:28:56.690
Thank you.

00:28:59.530 --> 00:28:59.850
Why?

00:29:00.020 --> 00:29:01.660
just hand me the board.

00:29:01.800 --> 00:29:04.440
Why does it say slave hands board to master?

00:29:05.370 --> 00:29:07.710
My world, it'll touch you today, ain't we?

00:29:08.210 --> 00:29:09.670
God, I got this nagging headache.

00:29:11.380 --> 00:29:13.520
Never mind, I'll take the board myself.

00:29:13.800 --> 00:29:15.960
Would it be too much trouble if I asked you for some nails?

00:29:16.890 --> 00:29:18.290
Anything you say, master.

00:29:19.100 --> 00:29:20.400
Just give me the nails.

00:29:25.980 --> 00:29:26.780
Oh, don't!

00:29:28.120 --> 00:29:29.620
in your pocket, not in your mouth.

00:29:31.700 --> 00:29:33.980
Honestly, I don't know how I've worked with you all these years.

00:29:34.380 --> 00:29:35.960
Get a new guy on the job, and he sees you

00:29:35.960 --> 00:29:37.320
do something filthy like that.

00:29:37.520 --> 00:29:37.800
Yeah.

00:29:39.820 --> 00:29:40.800
Thank you.

00:29:42.820 --> 00:29:44.080
Don't put him back in the keg!

00:29:44.550 --> 00:29:46.830
Other people got a nail out of that keg, you know.

00:29:47.180 --> 00:29:48.040
Hey you

00:29:48.870 --> 00:29:51.330
Will you show him where carpenters keep their nails?

00:29:56.650 --> 00:29:57.450
Come on, give me a hand.

00:29:58.090 --> 00:29:58.290
Yes.

00:29:59.300 --> 00:29:59.960
I'd be happy.

00:30:00.310 --> 00:30:01.450
Come on, let's get going.

00:30:01.750 --> 00:30:03.190
Wasted enough time already.

00:30:03.490 --> 00:30:03.770
Stop!

00:30:04.330 --> 00:30:05.330
What's the matter?

00:30:06.300 --> 00:30:08.220
I broke a fingernail, so what?

00:30:09.020 --> 00:30:11.700
So what? You expect me to play darts tonight with that?

00:30:12.220 --> 00:30:12.440
Thank you.

00:30:13.210 --> 00:30:14.810
Boy, are you a complainer?

00:30:14.930 --> 00:30:16.230
You're even worse than George.

00:30:16.490 --> 00:30:17.410
Never mind about George.

00:30:17.590 --> 00:30:18.570
I don't want to hear nothing about George.

00:30:18.690 --> 00:30:19.350
He's my best friend.

00:30:19.900 --> 00:30:20.560
Oh, is that right?

00:30:20.700 --> 00:30:20.940
Yeah.

00:30:21.200 --> 00:30:22.880
Well, how come I saw him at the ball game

00:30:22.880 --> 00:30:24.280
last Tuesday night with Harry?

00:30:25.990 --> 00:30:27.610
You lie, am I?

00:30:27.730 --> 00:30:29.470
Why don't you call him and find out for yourself?

00:30:30.060 --> 00:30:32.200
You know I can't call him now. He's down in the sewer.

00:30:32.740 --> 00:30:34.060
Well, it's true, anyway.

00:30:34.200 --> 00:30:34.660
You know what?

00:30:34.760 --> 00:30:35.520
You know what I think you are?

00:30:35.620 --> 00:30:35.720
What?

00:30:35.780 --> 00:30:37.980
You're nothing but a low-down, lying, vicious gossip.

00:30:38.040 --> 00:30:38.320
Oh, yeah.

00:30:38.340 --> 00:30:40.700
And I never want to speak to you again as long as I live.

00:30:40.820 --> 00:30:42.780
Well, that's just fine with me, buddy boy.

00:30:42.880 --> 00:30:44.540
Hey, hey, helper, come over here, ma'am.

00:30:44.740 --> 00:30:47.740
Will you tell Mr. Wilson there for him to go ahead and do his half,

00:30:47.800 --> 00:30:49.560
and I will do my half.

00:30:49.970 --> 00:30:52.870
Uh, he said, Mr. Wilson, that you should go ahead

00:30:52.870 --> 00:30:54.910
and do your half, and then he'll do his half.

00:30:54.930 --> 00:30:55.450
Yeah, yeah, yeah, OK.

00:30:55.530 --> 00:30:56.810
And you tell him that I will do my half,

00:30:56.870 --> 00:30:58.490
as long as he sees over there and does his half.

00:30:58.610 --> 00:30:59.970
And what's more, I will do my half.

